{"event_id": "evt_0016", "session": 1, "turn_no": 1, "world_time": "Sandbox d, night", "actor": "gm", "kind": "gm_narration", "summary": "Narration for amw8gvdpi3akv7g.", "visibility": "player", "knowledge_type": "fact", "known_to": [], "caused_by": [], "roll_ids": [], "tags": [], "details": {"text": "You haul the door round and it slams into the frame. Inside, the dog's claws skitter on the boards.\n\nYou set the tip of the blade to the seam where the latch strap meets the frame. The steel goes white, then runs. One tack. You draw the tip toward the next.\n\nThe door jumps under your left hand. A weight like a thrown sack hits it from the inside, and your arm folds. The door bursts outward, the half-made tack tearing loose in a spray of orange beads, and the dog is in the gap, a yard of black fur and teeth.\n\nIt lunges for you. You feel the breath of it on your forearm, hear the jaws clap shut on nothing.\n\nIt stands in the doorway, an arm's length away, head low, the open shed dark behind it. Wick is behind you; the lantern light shakes across the gravel.\n\nWhat do you do?\n"}, "idempotency_key": "amw8gvdpi3akv7g:narr"}
